00:44:50.120 --> 00:44:52.885
A big gingham...
a big gingham turban


00:44:53.080 --> 00:44:56.687
and very large hoop earrings
that I could wear


00:44:56.880 --> 00:45:00.965
with a nice crisp shirt
and blue jeans?


00:45:01.120 --> 00:45:03.885
They said to me,
"Don't you know


00:45:04.040 --> 00:45:06.088
young ladies
do not wearjeans?


00:45:06.240 --> 00:45:07.685
What's wrong with you?"


00:45:07.840 --> 00:45:09.922
And I said, "But I want a pair.
I need a pair."


00:45:10.080 --> 00:45:12.287
"Well, we're very sorry.
We can't help you."


00:45:12.480 --> 00:45:15.086
Well, they were just so mean.
They threw me out.


00:45:15.240 --> 00:45:17.971
But when I want something,
I'm like a dog with a bone,


00:45:18.120 --> 00:45:19.565
so I went back.


00:45:19.720 --> 00:45:21.484
I went back
a couple of times,


00:45:21.640 --> 00:45:24.450
and finally,
I guess in an effort


00:45:24.600 --> 00:45:26.728
just to get me off his back,


00:45:26.880 --> 00:45:29.201
the owner called me
on the telephone...


00:45:29.360 --> 00:45:31.567
Oh, it was maybe about
five or six weeks


00:45:31.720 --> 00:45:33.484
of really hard work
on my part...


00:45:33.640 --> 00:45:36.564
And he said
he had mail-order...


00:45:36.720 --> 00:45:40.281
had mail ordered me
a pair of boy's jeans,


00:45:40.440 --> 00:45:42.204
and they fit.


00:45:42.360 --> 00:45:44.886
So I put the outfit together,
and it was really smashing.


00:45:45.040 --> 00:45:46.166
It really was.


00:45:46.320 --> 00:45:49.608
Do you think, Iris, like,
for you, did...


00:45:49.760 --> 00:45:52.161
Because for me,
I became confident


00:45:52.320 --> 00:45:54.243
once I, like,
pretended I was


00:45:54.400 --> 00:45:57.165
and forced myself into wearing
things I was shy about.


00:45:57.320 --> 00:45:59.926
Did it come after
for you or...


00:46:00.080 --> 00:46:02.082
I can't remember
that far back.


00:46:13.800 --> 00:46:15.689
Hey, sweetheart,
you look beautiful as ever.


00:46:15.840 --> 00:46:17.808
Thank you.
I'm vertical, so I'm so happy.


00:46:18.000 --> 00:46:19.764
Oh.
flaughs)


00:46:19.960 --> 00:46:21.564
You know why I think
you did this film?


00:46:21.720 --> 00:46:23.529
- Why?
- Because he's very handsome,


00:46:23.680 --> 00:46:25.523
and I think
you really had a crush on him.


00:46:25.720 --> 00:46:27.484
- Everybody does.
- I know.


00:46:27.680 --> 00:46:30.365
Remember the evening
we went to that party,


00:46:30.520 --> 00:46:32.841
and there were a number
of elderly ladies,


00:46:33.000 --> 00:46:36.243
and they were like...
all over Albert.


00:46:36.400 --> 00:46:39.210
- Yeah.
- My God. He was like a magnet.


00:46:39.400 --> 00:46:41.607
Uaughs)


00:46:41.760 --> 00:46:45.401
Isn't it amazing now
how many designers don't sew?


00:46:45.560 --> 00:46:47.608
They don't sew.
They don't drape.


00:46:47.760 --> 00:46:50.684
- They're media freaks.
- Right, exactly, yeah.


00:46:50.840 --> 00:46:53.081
It's unbelievable.


00:46:53.240 --> 00:46:55.686
See, these new kids
go to the vintage shows,


00:46:55.840 --> 00:46:59.049
and they buy a few pieces,
and they change a button or two,


00:46:59.200 --> 00:47:01.362
and they knock it off,
and it's crazy.


00:47:01.520 --> 00:47:03.761
Theyjust have no sense
of history


00:47:03.960 --> 00:47:06.008
and no curiosity
about anything.


00:47:06.160 --> 00:47:08.049
When you were, like,
growing up,


00:47:08.200 --> 00:47:11.283
didn't you have a sense
of history just from reading


00:47:11.440 --> 00:47:12.805
- and looking at things...
- Oh, of course.


00:47:12.960 --> 00:47:14.325
Listening to music
and everything?


00:47:14.480 --> 00:47:18.246
I had a great sense of history,
and I realized


00:47:18.400 --> 00:47:20.641
that everything
is interrelated


00:47:20.800 --> 00:47:24.805
and that politics and science
and economics and fashion


00:47:24.960 --> 00:47:26.610
and all that are one
and part of the same,


00:47:26.760 --> 00:47:30.651
and I applied it...
I know if you look at a dress,


00:47:30.800 --> 00:47:33.485
it's affected
by all those things.


00:47:33.640 --> 00:47:36.849
I mean, you can almost tell what
was going on at that period.


00:47:37.040 --> 00:47:39.247
You know,
I've never heard you say,


00:47:39.400 --> 00:47:40.925
"l don't like the way
that person dresses."


00:47:41.080 --> 00:47:43.401
- I can't sit in judgment.
- Right, exactly.


00:47:43.560 --> 00:47:45.005
- It's not my business.
- Right.


00:47:45.160 --> 00:47:46.571
If they're happy that way...
you know,


00:47:46.720 --> 00:47:48.609
It's better to be happy
than well-dressed.


00:47:48.800 --> 00:47:51.883
Flaughs)
Exactly. That's so great.


00:48:08.280 --> 00:48:09.566
Nice.


00:48:34.800 --> 00:48:37.246
- Hi.
- There she is.


00:48:37.400 --> 00:48:39.209
Hi.
Oh, how cute.


00:48:39.360 --> 00:48:41.249
Welcome, you're so...


00:48:41.560 --> 00:48:44.245
Okay, Iris,
after this is all laid out,


00:48:44.440 --> 00:48:46.681
I am officiallyjealous.


00:48:46.840 --> 00:48:49.047
I have a lot
of catching up to do.


00:48:49.200 --> 00:48:51.123
- No, I mean...
- This is a drop in the bucket.


00:48:53.280 --> 00:48:56.045
Okay, so Iris and everybody,
can I tell you what we set up?


00:48:56.240 --> 00:48:57.287
All the accessories are here.


00:48:57.440 --> 00:48:59.283
All the shoes
are down on the floor.


00:48:59.440 --> 00:49:01.647
I'm not sure if we're going to
get that far, but they're there.


00:49:01.800 --> 00:49:05.247
We dressed several mannequins
here with almost everything...


00:49:05.400 --> 00:49:07.368
Right behind you.
...almost everything.


00:49:07.520 --> 00:49:10.649
- This one I...
- You tell us what to do.


00:49:10.840 --> 00:49:13.571
And this I thought
with the brown pants.


00:49:13.760 --> 00:49:15.888
- The brown pants?
- Yeah, that's so you don't...


00:49:16.040 --> 00:49:18.281
- You don't see anything else.
- Okay.


00:49:18.440 --> 00:49:22.843
And then I have some jewelry.
And I have those Missoni shoes.


00:49:26.280 --> 00:49:28.169
And then I put this...


00:49:28.640 --> 00:49:30.005
- That on top of that?
- Yeah.


00:49:30.160 --> 00:49:33.846
Oh, that's the secret for
how you get some of your depth.


00:49:34.640 --> 00:49:36.802
Beautiful, so sculptural.


00:49:37.560 --> 00:49:39.847
- It spoils the...
- The line of the jacket?


00:49:39.960 --> 00:49:41.041
- Yeah.
- Okay.


00:49:41.120 --> 00:49:42.485
Is she dragging it?


00:49:42.640 --> 00:49:45.086
Yeah, that's what I mean,
something like that.


00:49:45.240 --> 00:49:46.480
Dragging it along kind of?


00:49:46.640 --> 00:49:47.641
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah,
I love that.


00:49:47.800 --> 00:49:50.531
- Because we can do that.
- That's what I meant.


00:49:50.680 --> 00:49:52.921
We like that kind of rhythm
anyway to break it up.


00:49:53.080 --> 00:49:55.401
So it'll go down here,
okay.


00:49:55.560 --> 00:49:58.484
- We think on the same beam.
- See?


00:50:00.680 --> 00:50:02.967
We could do, you know,


00:50:03.120 --> 00:50:05.771
glitz and bling
if you wanted to,


00:50:05.920 --> 00:50:08.082
or we could just do
this kind of...


00:50:08.240 --> 00:50:09.605
Lots and lots of dots, right.


00:50:09.760 --> 00:50:12.127
Iris, that looks pretty great.


00:50:12.320 --> 00:50:14.607
You know you could do...
maybe want to add this to it?


00:50:14.760 --> 00:50:16.489
Oh, I see how this works.


00:50:19.960 --> 00:50:22.088
Some people might have assumed
this was just one piece.


00:50:22.240 --> 00:50:25.130
- People usually do.
- But no, you're making it.


00:50:25.280 --> 00:50:27.362
What you have to do...
see, I used to do things


00:50:27.520 --> 00:50:32.890
with antique bits and pieces,
and what I was so proud of


00:50:33.040 --> 00:50:34.883
was they looked like
they were born that way.


00:50:35.040 --> 00:50:36.849
They didn't look like
they were put together.


00:50:37.000 --> 00:50:38.331
I hate when
it looks put together.


00:50:40.920 --> 00:50:42.888
Oh, you want this
on the top here.


00:50:43.040 --> 00:50:44.246
- Yeah.
- Okay.


00:50:44.400 --> 00:50:46.243
Or you think maybe
too much for the window?


00:50:46.400 --> 00:50:47.731
No! no! no, "Q, "C.


00:50:47.880 --> 00:50:49.609
You know the secret
behind doing windows?


00:50:49.760 --> 00:50:52.206
- What, too much?
- No, it's never too much.


00:50:52.400 --> 00:50:54.801
You always do
the most outlandish.


00:50:54.960 --> 00:50:58.248
Oh, well, that's for me.
You want to give me a job?


00:50:58.800 --> 00:51:00.245
Iris,
let me ask you a question.


00:51:00.400 --> 00:51:02.687
Do you have glasses to spare?


00:51:02.840 --> 00:51:04.604
Well, for the window,
I guess I have a few pairs.


00:51:04.760 --> 00:51:06.171
I don't know how many I have.


00:51:06.320 --> 00:51:08.687
We were thinking we might
do this sort of thing.


00:51:08.840 --> 00:51:12.686
See it, Linda, the mask there?
Might do something like that.


00:51:13.240 --> 00:51:15.925
- This is a classic...
- I kind of like the glasses.


00:51:18.880 --> 00:51:20.609
The mannequins
could be holding something.


00:51:20.800 --> 00:51:23.041
I think it's a little chicer
just with glasses


00:51:23.200 --> 00:51:24.850
instead of with...
you know what I mean?


00:51:25.000 --> 00:51:27.048
We know it's Iris
just by the glasses.


00:51:27.200 --> 00:51:28.565
Let's just...


00:51:29.240 --> 00:51:30.685
but these would break, I guess.


00:51:30.840 --> 00:51:33.002
Here, I'm not going to
let go of them.


00:51:36.520 --> 00:51:39.046
Let's see the...
Let's try this girl here.


00:51:43.000 --> 00:51:44.684
Gee, I wonder who this is.


00:52:14.840 --> 00:52:16.729
The point of this
is just a little thing.


00:52:16.880 --> 00:52:19.770
I wanted to show sort of
all your different jobs,


00:52:19.920 --> 00:52:22.491
that you have
more jobs than anyone.


00:52:24.160 --> 00:52:27.164
Oh, I love that.
I love that.


00:52:28.600 --> 00:52:29.886
Isn't there sound?


00:52:30.080 --> 00:52:32.924
How do we tell the man
that there's no sound?


00:52:33.080 --> 00:52:34.570
Oh, okay, thanks.


00:52:35.240 --> 00:52:37.083
Can you start it over?


00:52:44.880 --> 00:52:46.530
We have something
really big for you


00:52:46.720 --> 00:52:48.006
- to surprise you with.
- For me?


00:52:48.160 --> 00:52:50.003
- Yes, absolutely.
- Oh, wow.


00:52:52.520 --> 00:52:55.205
There's some noise
coming from the bag.


00:52:56.120 --> 00:52:59.681
o“, my God! oh!


00:52:59.840 --> 00:53:02.002
So you can use this
to shop with you


00:53:02.160 --> 00:53:04.970
when you go to Whole Foods
to buy your forbidden rice.


00:53:05.160 --> 00:53:06.446
Oh, that's fabulous!


00:53:06.600 --> 00:53:09.251
- That's going to be in the stores.
- No.


00:53:09.400 --> 00:53:10.731
- Yeah.
- Big like this?


00:53:10.880 --> 00:53:13.406
- Big like this.
- Oh, Albert, look at that.


00:53:13.560 --> 00:53:16.325
- Oh, my God.
- We're excited about it.


00:53:16.480 --> 00:53:19.211
Oh.


00:53:19.360 --> 00:53:22.842
Oh, I can't believe it.
Oh, my God.


00:53:23.360 --> 00:53:24.850
I love you, Rory.


00:53:25.000 --> 00:53:27.731
You've been so kind
and gracious to me.


00:53:28.280 --> 00:53:29.566
My God.


00:53:29.720 --> 00:53:31.688
If somebody could
just open the door?


00:53:31.840 --> 00:53:33.251
I'll get it.


00:53:35.840 --> 00:53:38.081
I heard your other
collection is sold out.


00:53:38.240 --> 00:53:39.241
Sold out.


00:53:39.360 --> 00:53:42.125
Yeah, the Home Shopping.
Yeah, it was so exciting.


00:53:42.320 --> 00:53:44.687
Were you on it yourself
selling it?


00:53:44.840 --> 00:53:46.922
I was supposed to,
and I was in the hospital.


00:53:47.080 --> 00:53:49.321
Ijust had surgery.


00:53:49.960 --> 00:53:52.167
So they asked me
if I would talk,


00:53:52.320 --> 00:53:55.688
and I said yes,
and I summoned all my energy,


00:53:55.840 --> 00:53:57.046
and I did two shows.


00:53:57.200 --> 00:53:59.521
I guess it was about
half an hour each.


00:54:00.200 --> 00:54:03.602
And I was very...
You know, it was very exciting,


00:54:03.800 --> 00:54:06.326
and the next... for two days,
I couldn't get out of bed


00:54:06.480 --> 00:54:08.448
I was so drained.


00:54:08.640 --> 00:54:10.404
Carl doesn't know
I had hip surgery.


00:54:10.600 --> 00:54:12.329
He doesn't know
my hip was broken.


00:54:12.480 --> 00:54:14.687
Really?
How did you do that?


00:54:14.840 --> 00:54:16.365
Well, I didn't do it.
Nezzie did.


00:54:16.560 --> 00:54:18.528
Because Carl
is very devoted to me,


00:54:18.680 --> 00:54:20.808
particularly now that
he isn't feeling well,


00:54:20.960 --> 00:54:23.930
and she said if she was going
to stay with him,


00:54:24.080 --> 00:54:26.560
she couldn't tell him
because he'd go bananas.


00:54:26.720 --> 00:54:29.963
And he really was so upset
that I wasn't at home.


00:54:30.160 --> 00:54:31.889
- He knows I fell...
- Where did he think you were?


00:54:32.080 --> 00:54:33.366
No, he knows I fell.


00:54:33.520 --> 00:54:35.045
He was sleeping
when it happened.


00:54:35.200 --> 00:54:38.488
But when he got up...
what was I going to do?


00:54:38.640 --> 00:54:41.211
I was trying to wait
till the next day,


00:54:41.360 --> 00:54:44.921
but the head of NYU,
the head honcho


00:54:45.080 --> 00:54:46.844
is a good friend,
and he said, "You're crazy.


00:54:47.000 --> 00:54:48.240
You have to come immediately,


00:54:48.400 --> 00:54:50.129
and you have to come
in an ambulance."


00:54:50.840 --> 00:54:53.161
So I had to call the ambulance,
and I thought, "Oh, my God."


00:54:53.320 --> 00:54:54.765
But God was good,


00:54:54.920 --> 00:54:57.400
and they sent me
the two most delicious guys.


00:54:57.600 --> 00:55:00.843
They were big hunks, but they
were so sweet and so kind.


00:55:01.000 --> 00:55:04.721
And I explained the situation,
and they were, you know,


00:55:04.880 --> 00:55:07.690
kidding around
with Carl and whatnot,


00:55:07.840 --> 00:55:09.205
and they got me out.


00:55:09.360 --> 00:55:10.361
He thinks I fell...


00:55:10.520 --> 00:55:12.887
He knows I fell
and hurt my leg badly,


00:55:13.080 --> 00:55:14.081
but he doesn't know
I broke my hip.


00:55:14.240 --> 00:55:15.287
He doesn't know what happened.


00:55:15.440 --> 00:55:16.771
So we're always together.


00:55:16.920 --> 00:55:18.445
We work together
and everything else,


00:55:18.600 --> 00:55:20.284
so he's used
to having me around.


00:55:20.440 --> 00:55:23.603
He's older than I am,
well, so it was very sweet.


00:55:23.760 --> 00:55:25.205
You're very sweet together.


00:55:25.360 --> 00:55:26.521
<i>AnyWaY---</i>


00:55:34.800 --> 00:55:36.689
Have you met...
This is the Maysles crew.


00:55:36.840 --> 00:55:38.604
- No!
- I'm Katie.


00:55:38.760 --> 00:55:41.604
Katie, I'm Nancy.
Nice to meet you.


00:55:41.760 --> 00:55:44.206
- Sean.
- Sean, nice to meet you.


00:55:44.880 --> 00:55:47.167
And this is Albert Maysles
himself.


00:55:47.360 --> 00:55:49.886
Hello, Albert,
so nice to meet you.


00:55:50.040 --> 00:55:51.326
You want a nibble?
Help yourself.


00:55:51.480 --> 00:55:53.881
- Yes, yes.
- Albert, you want...


00:55:54.040 --> 00:55:56.042
I'm okay.
I had some breakfast.


00:55:56.200 --> 00:55:58.806
- Sweetie, you want some?
- We're okay, thank you.


00:55:59.000 --> 00:56:01.207
Greetings,
and welcome to the launch


00:56:01.360 --> 00:56:03.249
of the UT in NYC program.


00:56:03.400 --> 00:56:07.291
It is my pleasure
to introduce Mrs. Iris Apfel,


00:56:07.440 --> 00:56:09.204
our tour guide
and visiting professor


00:56:09.360 --> 00:56:11.203
for the week
in New York City.


00:56:11.360 --> 00:56:13.089
Mrs. Apfel?


00:56:13.240 --> 00:56:16.323
I have brought you
14 eager students


00:56:16.480 --> 00:56:18.050
from the University of Texas.


00:56:18.200 --> 00:56:19.964
Good, well, I don't want
to waste any time


00:56:20.120 --> 00:56:22.282
because we have
a lot of things to do.


00:56:22.480 --> 00:56:25.848
And the reason I chose this
was because I've had occasion


00:56:26.000 --> 00:56:28.446
in the last couple of years
to work with students,


00:56:28.600 --> 00:56:31.524
which I never did before,
and I find that, unhappily,


00:56:31.680 --> 00:56:33.921
they may be very well-trained
in their craft,


00:56:34.080 --> 00:56:36.970
but they haven't got a clue
as to the outside world.


00:56:38.320 --> 00:56:40.482
So the sage has spoken.


00:56:47.280 --> 00:56:49.760
Everybody faints
when they hear the itinerary


00:56:49.920 --> 00:56:51.763
because it's really...
I must say,


00:56:51.920 --> 00:56:55.402
they're all offbeat fields
like licensing and styling


00:56:55.560 --> 00:56:58.086
and things that kids
don't think about as fashion.


00:56:58.240 --> 00:56:59.890
They just think
it's not glamorous,


00:57:00.040 --> 00:57:01.769
but it's important.


00:57:01.920 --> 00:57:05.288
I mean, all the great
handcrafted trades


00:57:05.480 --> 00:57:06.606
are going down the tubes.


00:57:06.760 --> 00:57:08.489
Some have already gone.


00:57:09.120 --> 00:57:10.929
And then there's nobody left
to teach them,


00:57:11.080 --> 00:57:15.085
and you'll have all kinds
of machine-made junk.


00:57:15.280 --> 00:57:18.489
Listen up, everybody,
this wonderful, wonderful man


00:57:18.640 --> 00:57:20.290
is going to talk with you.


00:57:20.440 --> 00:57:23.762
He is in my opinion,
and I think not only mine


00:57:23.960 --> 00:57:26.964
but everybody else's,
the king of the runway,


00:57:27.120 --> 00:57:29.043
and he comes
from a long tradition


00:57:29.200 --> 00:57:31.328
of embroiderers and beaders.


00:57:31.480 --> 00:57:33.767
So listen, he's going to
tell you wonderful things.


00:57:33.920 --> 00:57:37.811
You have to keep your eyes open
for anything and everything.


00:57:37.960 --> 00:57:42.409
Like me flying, going to Miami,
I look down from the plane,


00:57:42.600 --> 00:57:45.206
and I see fields of...
you know, fields.


00:57:45.360 --> 00:57:47.567
It looked like a...
like an amazing pattern.


00:57:47.720 --> 00:57:50.769
I drew it up,
and it's in one of my dresses.


00:57:50.920 --> 00:57:53.446
Now it's up to you
as a designer.


00:57:54.320 --> 00:57:56.049
What are you inspired by?


00:57:56.240 --> 00:57:58.322
And I think
whatever feeds you...


00:57:58.480 --> 00:57:59.686
You could be curious about math,


00:57:59.840 --> 00:58:01.001
you could be curious
about science,


00:58:01.200 --> 00:58:02.406
you could be curious
about fashion,


00:58:02.560 --> 00:58:03.721
you could be curious
about anything,


00:58:03.880 --> 00:58:05.769
but ultimately, what drives you
and makes you better


00:58:05.960 --> 00:58:07.325
is learning something
you don't already know.


00:58:07.480 --> 00:58:09.767
I could never be
a good friend of anybody


00:58:09.960 --> 00:58:12.247
who wasn't curious or didn't
have a sense of humor.


00:58:12.400 --> 00:58:15.210
I think those are the two great
gifts that I got in my cradle.


00:58:15.360 --> 00:58:16.407
I really believe that.


00:58:16.560 --> 00:58:19.484
People always love enthusiasm,
and I think that, in the end,


00:58:19.680 --> 00:58:22.411
New York is about work
and getting a job done.


00:58:22.600 --> 00:58:25.080
So it's great if you're
a cute girl in a cute dress


00:58:25.240 --> 00:58:27.481
and want to be
on the red carpet, but really,


00:58:27.640 --> 00:58:30.291
if you mean business,
New York is the place for you.


00:58:30.480 --> 00:58:31.481
If you mean business,


00:58:31.560 --> 00:58:33.289
people will
take you seriously, I think.


00:58:34.120 --> 00:58:36.771
It's very important to me
that my program continue.


00:58:36.920 --> 00:58:39.082
It's going gangbusters.


00:58:39.280 --> 00:58:43.729
The kids are now fighting to get
in, and the school shows no...


00:58:43.880 --> 00:58:46.326
I mean, unless it falls
by the wayside


00:58:46.480 --> 00:58:48.164
and they can't get
anymore funding...


00:58:48.320 --> 00:58:50.402
I mean,
I can't do this forever,


00:58:50.560 --> 00:58:52.324
but I'm sure they'll be able
to get somebody else.


00:58:52.480 --> 00:58:53.925
Awesome, thank you.


00:58:58.240 --> 00:59:00.447
You never had children.


00:59:00.640 --> 00:59:02.369
No, we never wanted to.


00:59:03.080 --> 00:59:04.730
I mean, not that I...
but you can't...


00:59:04.880 --> 00:59:07.804
I learned a long time ago you
can't have everything,


00:59:07.960 --> 00:59:11.009
and I wanted a career,
and I wanted to travel,


00:59:11.160 --> 00:59:13.527
and my mother...
I know how much I resented it.


00:59:13.680 --> 00:59:15.682
She had stopped for a while,


00:59:15.840 --> 00:59:18.491
and then when I was like ten
or 11, she went back,


00:59:18.640 --> 00:59:22.850
and I was very upset.
Very upset.


00:59:23.000 --> 00:59:24.650
I felt I was...
I mean, it was stupid,


00:59:24.800 --> 00:59:26.404
but I felt I was being
abandoned,


00:59:26.560 --> 00:59:31.248
so I said I didn't want to have
my child raised by a nanny.


00:59:31.400 --> 00:59:34.290
And you can't do everything.
It's impossible.


00:59:34.800 --> 00:59:36.484
Something has to give.


00:59:37.240 --> 00:59:38.890
And sometimes it's you.


00:59:43.000 --> 00:59:46.288
Well, I haven't had a
chance to go through anything.


00:59:46.440 --> 00:59:47.521
Yes.


00:59:47.680 --> 00:59:49.284
Logistics, logistics.


00:59:53.120 --> 00:59:54.804
Okay. There we go.


00:59:56.200 --> 00:59:58.771
Galliano's pieces
are fantastic.


00:59:58.920 --> 01:00:00.524
Yes.


01:00:03.040 --> 01:00:05.247
This is spectacular.


01:00:06.120 --> 01:00:10.125
The Peabody Essex Museum
hosted Iris' exhibition


01:00:10.280 --> 01:00:13.363
"The Rare Bird of Fashion"
in, um...


01:00:13.520 --> 01:00:14.646
'09.


01:00:15.080 --> 01:00:18.004
And then when the
exhibition came to the museum,


01:00:18.160 --> 01:00:19.730
we invited Iris and Carl,
of course,


01:00:19.880 --> 01:00:22.360
to be part
of the installation.


01:00:22.520 --> 01:00:25.842
And so I learned
that Peabody


01:00:26.000 --> 01:00:29.447
had a fashion collection,
but it more or less stopped


01:00:29.640 --> 01:00:31.369
at the time that mine begins.


01:00:31.960 --> 01:00:34.406
So we decided
that it would be a nice fit,


01:00:34.560 --> 01:00:37.245
and that I would,
little by little,


01:00:37.440 --> 01:00:39.886
give all the stuff
to the museum.


01:00:40.040 --> 01:00:42.042
So we started last year.


01:00:42.240 --> 01:00:43.890
They got 80-odd pieces
last year.


01:00:44.040 --> 01:00:45.121
Yes, mm-hmm.


01:00:45.200 --> 01:00:48.727
Probably get another batch,
and will keep going.


01:00:48.880 --> 01:00:52.601
Oh, those are trousers.
Oh, look at that.


01:00:53.040 --> 01:00:55.441
Oh, with a matching coat.


01:00:58.920 --> 01:01:01.526
What an interesting
color combination.


01:01:01.720 --> 01:01:03.563
This is a very personal
collection.


01:01:03.760 --> 01:01:07.207
This is mine, and I didn't
buy it to impress anybody.


01:01:07.360 --> 01:01:09.362
I bought it
because I liked it.


01:01:09.560 --> 01:01:11.722
And I wore almost everything.


01:01:13.560 --> 01:01:15.881
Some things I wore to pieces.


01:01:16.040 --> 01:01:18.247
This is the green...
This is the green one.


01:01:18.440 --> 01:01:23.207
I was collecting
church vestments at one point.


01:01:23.360 --> 01:01:27.126
So with this one,
I found a pair.


01:01:27.280 --> 01:01:29.965
I took the pair,
and I cut it apart,


01:01:30.160 --> 01:01:32.128
and I made a pair of trousers.


01:01:32.920 --> 01:01:35.651
- This has a number.
- What is that?


01:01:35.800 --> 01:01:38.041
It's a black, white,
or blue...


01:01:38.200 --> 01:01:40.407
- With fringe.
- Oh, no, it's dark blue.


01:01:40.560 --> 01:01:43.723
Oh, that's a gorgeous fabric.
That is a fabric to die for.


01:01:43.880 --> 01:01:48.522
Yeah, as if there aren't other
to-die-for fabrics here.


01:01:48.720 --> 01:01:49.801
But this one is very...


01:01:49.960 --> 01:01:51.041
But it's interesting
to see which ones


01:01:51.200 --> 01:01:53.282
you get really excited about.


01:01:54.320 --> 01:01:55.367
Look at this.


01:01:55.560 --> 01:01:57.722
- Oh, wow.
- It's woven.


01:01:57.880 --> 01:02:00.042
It's a velvet
and then the lace, wow.


01:02:00.520 --> 01:02:01.851
It's quite the combination.


01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:04.844
But look at how it's threaded
up through with the fringe.


01:02:05.000 --> 01:02:07.287
Where did you find this?
Here or...


01:02:07.440 --> 01:02:10.284
No, you' don't find
anything like this here.


01:02:10.440 --> 01:02:13.842
Somebody once told me,
and it's so true,


01:02:14.040 --> 01:02:15.565
you really don't own
anything while you're here.


01:02:15.720 --> 01:02:17.609
You just rent,
so sometimes,


01:02:17.760 --> 01:02:19.967
it might be nicer to
see where it's going


01:02:20.120 --> 01:02:23.841
than to not know who gets it,
so I'm happy to do it.


01:02:37.840 --> 01:02:40.241
How do you choose
what to give away?


01:02:40.440 --> 01:02:42.442
It's not easy.


01:02:42.600 --> 01:02:44.443
Does it keep you up?


01:02:45.360 --> 01:02:47.203
Oh, God, no.


01:02:49.200 --> 01:02:52.727
No, I have more important things
to keep me up at night.


01:02:52.880 --> 01:02:54.325
No, no.


01:02:54.480 --> 01:02:56.403
Well,
now I have to ask what...


01:02:56.560 --> 01:02:58.130
What keeps you up at night?


01:02:59.160 --> 01:03:01.083
Oh, I mean...


01:03:02.240 --> 01:03:04.925
Matters of health
and things like that.


01:03:06.320 --> 01:03:07.606
Things
that are really important.


01:03:07.800 --> 01:03:09.131
Mm-hmm.


01:03:11.360 --> 01:03:12.771
I mean, as you get older,
you realize


01:03:12.920 --> 01:03:15.127
that all these other things
are just...


01:03:25.840 --> 01:03:27.729
Iris,
just looking over here?


01:03:32.400 --> 01:03:35.051
How many people have been
in here before, Iris?


01:03:35.200 --> 01:03:37.328
Not too many.
I don't let anybody in here.


01:03:37.480 --> 01:03:39.642
Trying to get it
a little organized.


01:03:40.480 --> 01:03:41.606
Great.


01:03:42.040 --> 01:03:43.724
Uaughs)


01:03:46.040 --> 01:03:47.485
Great.


01:03:48.560 --> 01:03:50.244
Do you want me
to hang this somewhere?


01:03:50.400 --> 01:03:51.925
- Just stick it here.
- Okay.


01:03:52.080 --> 01:03:54.845
I have two more hangars
of items.


01:03:55.000 --> 01:03:56.206
Thank you.


01:04:00.120 --> 01:04:02.964
It's a system until a lot
of people stick their noses in,


01:04:03.120 --> 01:04:05.726
and then it gets
all fucked up.


01:04:07.760 --> 01:04:08.886
Put it here.


01:04:09.040 --> 01:04:11.520
Okay, and then
this J. Crew dress.


01:04:11.680 --> 01:04:13.284
- Put it here.
- Okay.


01:04:14.360 --> 01:04:15.441
Look at that coat.


01:04:15.600 --> 01:04:18.046
Hi.
How are you?


01:04:18.200 --> 01:04:19.440
My beautiful child.


01:04:19.600 --> 01:04:20.840
How are you, pussycat?


01:04:27.560 --> 01:04:28.561
I made it.


01:04:28.760 --> 01:04:31.843
Are you all right?
Are you okay?


01:04:32.000 --> 01:04:33.490
I don't know.


01:04:33.680 --> 01:04:35.648
Somebody's stealing my breath.


01:04:35.800 --> 01:04:38.929
Be quiet.
Relax, relax, relax.


01:04:44.600 --> 01:04:47.524
What's that cousin's name
with two kids up there?


01:04:47.680 --> 01:04:51.162
Carl, just relax.
Don't talk.


01:04:52.040 --> 01:04:53.690
Catch your breath.


01:04:54.280 --> 01:04:55.850
My aunt rarely relaxes,


01:04:56.000 --> 01:04:58.571
and I think that's kind
of a fault on occasion.


01:04:58.720 --> 01:05:02.327
I think sometimes she should
slow down, and I ask her,


01:05:02.480 --> 01:05:04.960
or I kind of even insist,
that she do a little bit,


01:05:05.120 --> 01:05:07.691
rests a little bit more,
but it's not her personality.


01:05:07.880 --> 01:05:09.644
She's even said
that when she's not busy,


01:05:09.840 --> 01:05:11.080
she can get depressed.


01:05:11.240 --> 01:05:12.651
She's not at all
a depressive person,


01:05:12.840 --> 01:05:14.444
but I can understand
that her personality


01:05:14.600 --> 01:05:17.524
is to keep moving,
keep busy, keep occupied,


01:05:17.720 --> 01:05:20.769
keep creative, keep productive,
and that's her life,


01:05:20.920 --> 01:05:22.649
and it has always been
her life.


01:05:30.640 --> 01:05:32.244
Oh, I like being active.


01:05:32.400 --> 01:05:34.243
I like being in the world
and of the world,


01:05:34.400 --> 01:05:37.483
and everybody has to do it
in his or her own way.


01:05:37.640 --> 01:05:39.847
I think I told you this
about my mother's friend.


01:05:40.040 --> 01:05:42.202
When you would say,
"How are you feeling today?"


01:05:42.360 --> 01:05:44.249
She'd say,
"Well, to tell you the truth,


01:05:44.400 --> 01:05:46.687
when I get up in the morning,
everything I have two of,


01:05:46.880 --> 01:05:49.645
one hurts,"
and that's the way it is.


01:05:49.840 --> 01:05:51.524
When you're older,
a lot of people


01:05:51.680 --> 01:05:54.126
just give into that,


01:05:54.280 --> 01:05:56.442
but unless it's something
really serious,


01:05:56.640 --> 01:05:59.120
but if it isn't,
you just have to push yourself,


01:05:59.280 --> 01:06:00.805
and then you go out,
and you start to do things,


01:06:00.960 --> 01:06:02.325
you forget about yourself.


01:06:02.520 --> 01:06:04.249
Otherwise,
you can just sit there


01:06:04.400 --> 01:06:06.164
and brood all day long.


01:06:06.320 --> 01:06:08.527
I mean, you cannot do
what you did.


01:06:08.920 --> 01:06:11.207
People say what an energy
and everything I have,


01:06:11.400 --> 01:06:13.767
but it's nothing
like what I used to have.


01:06:14.600 --> 01:06:15.965
Now I get tired.


01:06:20.120 --> 01:06:22.202
I'm ready for the voyage.


01:06:25.840 --> 01:06:27.205
- Hi, sweetie.
- Hi, darling.


01:06:27.280 --> 01:06:28.361
How are you?


01:06:28.600 --> 01:06:30.523
I don't know. Vertical.
I'm vertical.


01:06:30.680 --> 01:06:32.603
- Where you going?
- Back to work.


01:06:32.800 --> 01:06:33.961
Back to work?


01:06:34.120 --> 01:06:36.487
Make sure they take it easy
with you, okay?


01:06:36.680 --> 01:06:39.286
- Yeah, they're good people.
- Okay.


01:06:46.000 --> 01:06:47.445
Hi.


01:06:47.600 --> 01:06:50.080
Okay, we're off and running.


01:07:09.800 --> 01:07:11.211
- Right here.
- Right here?


01:07:11.360 --> 01:07:12.930
Yeah, that's the elevator.


01:07:20.960 --> 01:07:22.849
Not a friendly policeman.


01:07:32.960 --> 01:07:34.371
Hello?


01:07:45.160 --> 01:07:47.561
I had a very
interesting clientele.


01:07:47.720 --> 01:07:50.326
They didn't want to be dragged
from showroom to showroom


01:07:50.480 --> 01:07:52.244
and have things
that everybody else had,


01:07:52.400 --> 01:07:54.721
so that started me traveling,


01:07:54.920 --> 01:07:56.809
and I went twice a year
to Europe


01:07:56.960 --> 01:07:59.611
and each time took at least
a 40-foot container


01:07:59.800 --> 01:08:02.804
besides going to all
the auctions and estate sales


01:08:02.960 --> 01:08:04.325
and everything else.


01:08:06.160 --> 01:08:08.845
That has to go.
That one goes.


01:08:09.000 --> 01:08:12.766
- And, uh, this piece goes.
- That one's going.


01:08:12.920 --> 01:08:15.730
Then, uh...
And two more pieces over there.


01:08:15.880 --> 01:08:18.406
Oh, a lot of pieces.


01:08:20.080 --> 01:08:22.162
I believe this one goes.


01:08:22.960 --> 01:08:26.362
That big long bench goes,
yes, yeah.


01:08:27.840 --> 01:08:29.808
It wasn't easy
to part with these things


01:08:30.000 --> 01:08:32.970
because they have so many
memories connected with them.


01:08:33.120 --> 01:08:35.726
I'm sorry to see them gone,
but c'est la vie.


01:08:35.920 --> 01:08:37.604
They don't do me
any good here.


01:08:37.800 --> 01:08:39.404
They don't do anybody any good,
and they're so beautiful,


01:08:39.560 --> 01:08:41.608
they might as well brighten
somebody's life,


01:08:41.800 --> 01:08:44.167
and frankly,
I can use a few more shekels.


01:08:44.320 --> 01:08:47.722
- This is 750.
- What were you thinking?


01:08:47.880 --> 01:08:49.450
- What?
- What were you thinking?


01:08:49.640 --> 01:08:52.246
I don't know.
I have to check. I really do.


01:08:55.880 --> 01:08:57.484
Oh, my God.


01:08:58.560 --> 01:09:01.928
Oh, my God,
it's one of those panels.


01:09:02.080 --> 01:09:03.491
Mm-hmm.


01:09:12.680 --> 01:09:15.206
Wait, there was something
I had to show you.


01:09:15.760 --> 01:09:18.001
Hmm.
That's really different.


01:09:21.520 --> 01:09:23.329
I thought it could be
a wall hanging,


01:09:23.480 --> 01:09:25.881
or it could even...
maybe a bed thing


01:09:26.040 --> 01:09:28.771
- because that could tuck under.
- Hang over the bottom?


01:09:28.920 --> 01:09:31.161
Mm-hmm. Yeah, definitely.


01:09:32.040 --> 01:09:33.280
<i>0K3)!-</i>


01:09:35.680 --> 01:09:37.045
When I didn't know any better


01:09:37.200 --> 01:09:38.929
and we first went to Paris


01:09:39.080 --> 01:09:40.889
years and years ago
right after the war,


01:09:41.040 --> 01:09:42.644
the dealers would say,
"You must come


01:09:42.800 --> 01:09:45.485
early in the morning to my..."
they called them "my box,"


01:09:45.640 --> 01:09:48.849
and you'd have to get there,
like, 4:00 in the morning


01:09:49.000 --> 01:09:50.650
with a big searchlight,


01:09:50.800 --> 01:09:54.441
and it was always damp
and cold and miserable.


01:09:54.600 --> 01:09:57.968
And we did that for a while,
and then my husband said to me,


01:09:58.120 --> 01:09:59.963
"You know,
this is really stupid.


01:10:00.120 --> 01:10:02.441
You don't buy
what other people buy,


01:10:02.600 --> 01:10:04.762
and almost everything you buy,
you always say,


01:10:04.920 --> 01:10:06.684
"lt has to have
my name on it.


01:10:07.320 --> 01:10:08.890
If it's got your name on it,
baby,


01:10:09.040 --> 01:10:11.008
it's going to be here
at 11:00 in the morning."


01:10:13.120 --> 01:10:15.964
So that's what we continued
to do, and it worked.


01:10:16.120 --> 01:10:19.124
I still occasionally miss
that terribly.


01:10:31.200 --> 01:10:32.645
It's definitely
the end of an era.


01:10:32.800 --> 01:10:37.010
It's the end of another life.
It took me a long time.


01:10:37.160 --> 01:10:39.367
You have
to get yourself psyched.


01:10:39.520 --> 01:10:41.409
Especially a collection
like that, you know,


01:10:41.560 --> 01:10:44.211
every piece has a memory
because most of them


01:10:44.360 --> 01:10:47.091
were bought on trips
or different occasions.


01:10:47.240 --> 01:10:50.369
My accountant said to me,
"Just think of all the money


01:10:50.520 --> 01:10:53.205
you would've saved if you
had done this years ago."


01:10:53.360 --> 01:10:55.488
Well,
but I wasn't ready.


01:10:56.280 --> 01:10:59.727
I feel that for everything
there is a season.


01:11:00.560 --> 01:11:02.369
And I suppose that when I put
the last key in the door,


01:11:02.520 --> 01:11:04.284
I'll go home
and get hysterical.


01:11:04.440 --> 01:11:06.807
Right now, I'm managing.


01:11:27.000 --> 01:11:28.968
You got a birthday
coming up, huh?


01:11:29.120 --> 01:11:32.203
Yeah, August 4th.
That scares the hell out of me.


01:11:34.040 --> 01:11:36.247
What am I going to do
for an encore?


01:11:36.400 --> 01:11:38.289
Ah, me.


01:11:38.480 --> 01:11:40.960
Well, if you made it
this far, you can go further,


01:11:41.120 --> 01:11:42.849
that's my idea.


01:11:57.120 --> 01:11:58.451
Happy birthday.


01:12:01.040 --> 01:12:02.690
You're looking great.
I love your pants.


01:12:09.120 --> 01:12:10.531
I can't tell you how happy...


01:12:10.720 --> 01:12:14.042
Dr. Pritchard took care of us
for over 40 years.


01:12:14.200 --> 01:12:17.409
Jenna, oh, I'm so happy
to see you.


01:12:17.600 --> 01:12:18.965
Hi, how are you?


01:12:24.960 --> 01:12:27.088
Happy birthday, kid.


01:12:29.800 --> 01:12:31.564
Carl doesn't like
to talk too much,


01:12:31.720 --> 01:12:34.883
so he wants me to say
a word or two or four.


01:12:35.040 --> 01:12:36.371
Go ahead.


01:12:36.520 --> 01:12:39.091
He wants to thank everybody
for coming.


01:12:39.240 --> 01:12:40.651
It's so nice.


01:12:40.800 --> 01:12:43.804
We're so pleased
that you're all in our life.


01:12:44.000 --> 01:12:46.731
You've been so generous
in sharing


01:12:46.920 --> 01:12:49.446
so many wonderful things
with us all these years.


01:12:49.600 --> 01:12:53.286
And Carl feels the same way,
and he's very happy


01:12:53.440 --> 01:12:57.411
to be sailing
into his second century.


01:13:01.040 --> 01:13:02.565
And he has...


01:13:02.720 --> 01:13:05.530
He has a word of advice
to the guys.


01:13:05.680 --> 01:13:09.082
He says,
in the words of my grandpa,


01:13:09.880 --> 01:13:12.486
"A woman is
as old as she looks,


01:13:12.640 --> 01:13:16.247
but a man is never old
until he stops looking."


01:13:20.760 --> 01:13:21.921
Blow, Carl.


01:13:33.120 --> 01:13:37.091
I want to do more things
in this life


01:13:37.240 --> 01:13:39.447
with my child bride.


01:13:41.640 --> 01:13:46.202
And if the Lord lets me do it,


01:13:46.400 --> 01:13:48.164
I'll sure enjoy it.


01:13:48.920 --> 01:13:50.763
Why not?


01:13:51.280 --> 01:13:53.169
You got one trip.


01:14:02.480 --> 01:14:03.686
Now, you see?


01:14:03.840 --> 01:14:07.162
She thought
I was getting chilly.


01:14:07.320 --> 01:14:08.970
She's right.


01:14:36.920 --> 01:14:39.321
I never felt pretty.
I don't feel pretty now.


01:14:39.880 --> 01:14:44.602
I'm not a pretty person.
I don't like pretty.


01:14:45.080 --> 01:14:48.527
So I don't feel badly,
and I think it worked out well


01:14:48.680 --> 01:14:51.763
because I found
that, for instance,


01:14:51.960 --> 01:14:56.568
all the girls that I know
who were very pretty girls


01:14:56.760 --> 01:15:00.685
and got by on their looks,
as time went on


01:15:00.840 --> 01:15:02.365
and they faded...


01:15:02.720 --> 01:15:04.563
They were nothing.


01:15:05.640 --> 01:15:07.802
And they were very,
very disappointed.


01:15:07.960 --> 01:15:10.088
When you're somebody
like myself,


01:15:10.240 --> 01:15:13.130
in order to get around
and be attractive,


01:15:13.320 --> 01:15:15.766
you have to develop something,
you have to learn something,


01:15:15.920 --> 01:15:17.684
and you have to do something.


01:15:17.840 --> 01:15:20.320
So you become
a bit more interesting.


01:15:20.920 --> 01:15:22.888
And when you get older,
you get by on that.


01:15:23.440 --> 01:15:26.011
Anyway, I don't happen
to like pretty.


01:15:32.360 --> 01:15:34.124
Most of the world
is not with me,


01:15:34.280 --> 01:15:36.009
but I don't care.


01:15:36.520 --> 01:15:38.522
Okay, excuse me.
Help yourself.


01:15:38.720 --> 01:15:40.245
Have anything you want.


